the queried accumulator capability matches the independent backend policy table: true
Schedule.optop coverage:
  Split              covered by split-then-unroll, split-then-swap, split-then-vectorize-inner, split-then-vectorize-narrow
  Swap               covered by split-then-swap
  Retype             covered by retype-vectorized, split-then-vectorize-inner, split-then-vectorize-narrow, retype-workgroup-reduce, retype-workgroup, mixed-guard-workgroup, rng-vectorized, rng-workgroup-reduce, sibling-vectorized, sibling-workgroup-reduce, data-guard-vectorized, data-guard-workgroup-reduce
  Unroll             covered by unroll-annot, unroll-mat, unroll-outer-mat, rng-unroll, rng-unroll-mat
  Partition          covered by partition, partition-then-unroll, partition-outer
  Pad                covered by pad-then-unroll-mat
  Stage              out of scope: stages an OPERAND into shared memory: it changes where the reduction reads from, never where its accumulator lives
  Privatize          out of scope: gives a scratch node a per-thread copy, which is a parallelism decision about a different node than the one being accumulated
  Expand_zero        covered by tile-mma-fallback
  Tensorize          covered by tile-mma-fallback
  Fuse_epilogue      out of scope: splices a consumer AFTER the reduction's closing store, so the form it follows is whichever one this table already pins
  Split_reduce       covered by split-reduce
every Schedule.optop constructor is reached by a member that exists, or exempted with a reason: true
Low_level.axis_type coverage:
  Serial             covered by serial, decline-data-guard, decline-sibling-statement
  Unrolled           covered by unroll-annot, decline-sibling-unrolled, rng-unroll
  Vectorized         covered by retype-vectorized, split-then-vectorize-inner, split-then-vectorize-narrow, rng-vectorized, sibling-vectorized, data-guard-vectorized
  Workgroup          covered by retype-workgroup, mixed-guard-workgroup
  Workgroup_reduce   covered by retype-workgroup-reduce, rng-workgroup-reduce, sibling-workgroup-reduce, data-guard-workgroup-reduce
  Grid               out of scope: its fallback is the plain serial loop and NOT the localizing one — the one arm that serializes without localizing. No schedule op in the tree produces an unbindable, non-parallel-eligible Grid level over a reduction axis, and one that existed would be a cross-thread race rather than a width question
every Low_level.axis_type constructor is reached by a member that exists, or exempted with a reason: true
the coverage samples name distinct constructors: true
the numerics policy is the default the member table's forms are stated for: true
reduction: out[3] = sum of 64 terms, hand-built Low_level, 36 members
  01 serial                      [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 no schedule ops (the reference rendering)                              -> localized scope
                                 codegen's peel takes one level, unguarded
  02 unroll-annot                [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Unroll (annotated: codegen repeats the body)                           -> localized scope
                                 codegen's peel takes one level, unguarded
  03 unroll-mat                  [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Unroll ~materialize (the schedule mints the scope)                     -> localized scope
                                 the scope is minted upstream; codegen's peel localizes nothing
  04 unroll-outer-mat            [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Unroll ~materialize of the OUTPUT axis                                 -> localized scope
                                 codegen's peel takes one level, unguarded
  05 partition                   [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Partition of the reduction axis into three segments                    -> localized scope
                                 the scope is minted upstream; codegen's peel localizes nothing
  06 partition-then-unroll       [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Partition, then Unroll one segment (the seam stays addressable)        -> localized scope
                                 the scope is minted upstream; codegen's peel localizes nothing
  07 partition-outer             [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Partition of the OUTPUT axis (the reduction is inside a segment)       -> localized scope
                                 codegen's peel takes one level, unguarded
  08 split-then-unroll           [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Split the reduction axis, then Unroll ~materialize the inner half      -> localized scope
                                 codegen's peel takes one level, unguarded
  09 split-then-swap             [f32         ] over plain                 Split the reduction axis, then Swap the halves                         -> localized scope
                                 codegen's peel takes 2 levels, unguarded
  10 pad-then-unroll-mat         [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Pad the reduction axis, then Unroll ~materialize (guarded copies)      -> localized scope
                                 the scope is minted upstream; codegen's peel localizes nothing
  11 split-reduce                [f32         ] over plain                 Split_reduce into four block partials plus a combine nest              -> scoped block partials + combine
                                 codegen's peel takes one level, unguarded
  12 retype-vectorized           [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Retype the reduction axis to Vectorized                                -> SIMD accumulator grid, or the localized scope where no vector rendering exists
                                 the shared width decision is wide and the SIMD grid holds it, or codegen's peel takes the reduction level where no vector rendering exists
  13 split-then-vectorize-inner  [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Split, then Retype the INNER half to Vectorized                        -> SIMD accumulator grid, or the localized scope where no vector rendering exists
                                 codegen's peel takes 2 levels, unguarded
  14 split-then-vectorize-narrow [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Split into a two-wide inner half, then Retype it Vectorized            -> localized scope
                                 codegen's peel takes 2 levels, unguarded
  15 retype-workgroup-reduce     [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Retype the reduction axis to Workgroup_reduce                          -> warp-shuffle tree, or the localized scope where no lane index is bound
                                 codegen peels the serialized level, or the shared width decision is wide and the shuffle tree holds it
  16 retype-workgroup            [f32 bf16 f16] over plain                 Retype the reduction axis to Workgroup (no index bound: serialized)    -> localized scope
                                 codegen's peel takes one level, unguarded
  17 runtime-guard               [f32 bf16 f16] over runtime-extent guard  a runtime-extent guard, unscheduled                                    -> localized scope
                                 codegen's peel takes one level, through a confined guard
  18 runtime-guard-unroll-mat    [f32 bf16 f16] over runtime-extent guard  a runtime-extent guard under Unroll ~materialize                       -> localized scope
                                 the scope is minted upstream; codegen's peel localizes nothing
  19 runtime-guard-partition     [f32 bf16 f16] over runtime-extent guard  a runtime-extent guard under Partition of the reduction axis           -> localized scope
                                 the scope is minted upstream; codegen's peel localizes nothing
  20 mixed-guard                 [f32 bf16 f16] over mixed lane guard      a guard mixing the enclosing output index with the peeled one          -> localized scope
                                 codegen's peel takes one level, through a lane-private guard
  21 mixed-guard-workgroup       [f32 bf16 f16] over mixed lane guard      the same guard with the output axis bound to a workgroup               -> localized scope
                                 codegen's peel takes one level, through a lane-private guard
  22 virtual-accumulator         [f32 bf16 f16] over virtual accumulator   a virtual accumulator inlined at its read site                         -> localized scope
                                 no cell recurrence at any level: the peel is never consulted
  23 where-guarded-update        [f32 bf16 f16] over Where-guarded scope   virtualization's Where-guarded update spelling                         -> localized scope
                                 no cell recurrence at any level: the peel is never consulted
  24 decline-data-guard          [f32 bf16 f16] over data-dependent guard  a data-dependent guard (not a pure index guard)                        -> per-step read-modify-write
                                 codegen's peel localizes nothing
  25 decline-sibling-statement   [f32 bf16 f16] over sibling statement     a second statement in the reduction level                              -> per-step read-modify-write
                                 codegen's peel localizes nothing
  26 decline-sibling-unrolled    [f32 bf16 f16] over sibling statement     the same level Unrolled: one read-modify-write per copy                -> per-step read-modify-write
                                 codegen's peel localizes nothing
  27 rng                         [bf16 f16    ] over RNG-bearing contribution an RNG-bearing contribution, unscheduled (the storage-pinned accumulator) -> per-step read-modify-write
                                 the shared width decision pins the accumulator to storage: nothing widens
  28 rng-unroll                  [bf16 f16    ] over RNG-bearing contribution the RNG-bearing level Unrolled: one read-modify-write per copy         -> per-step read-modify-write
                                 the shared width decision pins the accumulator to storage: nothing widens
  29 rng-unroll-mat              [bf16 f16    ] over RNG-bearing contribution the RNG-bearing level Unroll ~materialize (a storage-width scope)      -> localized scope
                                 the scope is minted upstream; codegen's peel localizes nothing
  30 rng-vectorized              [bf16 f16    ] over RNG-bearing contribution the RNG-bearing axis Retyped to Vectorized: the SIMD grid declines     -> per-step read-modify-write
                                 the shared width decision pins the accumulator to storage: nothing widens
  31 rng-workgroup-reduce        [bf16 f16    ] over RNG-bearing contribution the RNG-bearing axis Retyped to Workgroup_reduce (serialized: no lane index bound) -> per-step read-modify-write
                                 the shared width decision pins the accumulator to storage: nothing widens
  32 sibling-vectorized          [f32 bf16 f16] over sibling statement     a second statement in the level, Retyped to Vectorized                 -> per-step read-modify-write
                                 codegen's peel localizes nothing
  33 sibling-workgroup-reduce    [f32 bf16 f16] over sibling statement     a second statement in the level, Retyped to Workgroup_reduce (serialized) -> per-step read-modify-write
                                 codegen's peel localizes nothing
  34 data-guard-vectorized       [f32 bf16 f16] over data-dependent guard  a data-dependent guard, Retyped to Vectorized                          -> per-step read-modify-write
                                 codegen's peel localizes nothing
  35 data-guard-workgroup-reduce [f32 bf16 f16] over data-dependent guard  a data-dependent guard, Retyped to Workgroup_reduce (serialized)       -> per-step read-modify-write
                                 codegen's peel localizes nothing
  36 tile-mma-fallback           [f32 bf16 f16] over small contraction     Tensorize whose emission preconditions fail (transposed-B operands)    -> Tile_mma scalar fallback
                                 codegen's peel takes one level, unguarded
every member's peel claim is coherent with the form it claims: true
the f32 draw of the RNG members' key: 0x1.3c6ef2p-1
the bf16 draw of the RNG members' key: 0x1.3cp-1
the bf16 draw is the f32 draw narrowed to bf16: the conversion consumes the same 32 bits of the key on every backend (gh-ocannl-951): true
